accounting, are not reflected in our profits, less; (3) an allowance for=20
the tax that would be paid by Berkshire if these retained earnings of=20
investees had instead been distributed to us.  When tabulating "operating=
=20
earnings" here, we exclude purchase-accounting adjustments as well as=20
capital gains and other major non-recurring items.

